    feat(cjmp): changed Syntax of the Features Directivec
    
    Created-by: methadone
    Commit-by: methadone
    Merged-by: CangjiePL
    Description: ## Change Details (Required)
    
    Changed Syntax of the Features Directive.
    
    New Grammar for the features directive:
    ```
    /**
     * featureId
     *     : (Ident | ContextIdent) (DOT (Ident | ContextIdent))* ;
     *
     * featuresSet
     *     : LCURL NL*
     *     featureId NL* (COMMA NL* featureId NL*)*
     *     RCURL ;
     *
     * featuresDirective
     *     : annotationList? FEATURES NL*
     *     featuresSet
     *     end+ ;
     */
    ```
    Sample:
    ```cangjie
    features { os.linux, os.darwin }
    package default
    
    main() {
        println("Hello, world!")
    }
    ```
    
    Empty features set sample:
    
    ```cangjie
    features {}
    package default
    
    main() {
        println("Hello, world!")
    }
    ```
    
    Annotation `@NonProduct` for the features directive:
    
    ```cangjie
    @NonProducr
    features {}
    package cmp
    
    public common func Call(): Unit
    ```
    
    ### 该需求带来的价值、应用场景？
    
    The new syntax allows for explicitly declaring a directive with an empty feature set, which simplifies readability and allows for attaching new annotations to it.
    The `@NonProduct` annotation affects the `cjc --scan-dependency` output and adds a boolean field named `product`, which is used by cjpm.
    - Sample:
    ```cangjie
    @NonProduct
    features { os.linux }
    package src
    
    main() {
        println("Hello, world!")
    }
    ```
    ```bash
    cjc --scan-dependency -p .
    ```
    ```json
    {"package":"src","isMacro":false,"accessLevel":"public","dependencies":[],"features":["os.linux"],"product":false}
    ```
    
    
    1. "product": true -> means that source-set (see [source-set](https://gitcode.com/Cangjie/cangjie_docs/blob/main/docs/tools/source_en/cmd-tools/cjpm_manual.md#source-sets-and-their-configuration) definition) will produce binary output.
    2. "product": false -> means that source-set (see [source-set](https://gitcode.com/Cangjie/cangjie_docs/blob/main/docs/tools/source_en/cmd-tools/cjpm_manual.md#source-sets-and-their-configuration) definition) will not produce binary output.
    
